# Chat UX bans (do not reintroduce)

When the user says **remove** or we **replace** a UX, **delete the old path** — component,
wire-up, intercept, attach-menu row, i18n for that UI. Do not leave a second entry point that
can pop the old thing back. Do **not** reintroduce removed UX in later PRs, “polish”,
FEATURES grade-ups, or “parity” work.

## 1. No “Recalled N memories” chip
- Do **not** show a recalled / “✨ Recalled N memories” (or similar) chip on assistant messages.
- Backend may still send `recalled` for logging/metrics; the **mobile UI must not surface it**.
- Do not wire `showRecalledMemories`, `chat.recalled_memories`, or equivalent UI again.

## 2. No Show more / Show less on LLM (assistant) message bodies
- Assistant markdown/text must **not** fold with Show more / Show less.
- Keep `CollapsibleMessageBody` **`collapsible={false}`** for assistant bubbles (or omit folding).
- **Exception:** code blocks may keep their own Show more / Show less (`CodeBlock`).
- User-message folding is separate; do not “fix parity” by enabling assistant folding again.

When the user says **remove**, leave it removed. Do **not** bring these back in later PRs,
“polish”, FEATURES grade-ups, or “parity” work.

## 3. No project filter chips on Schedule
- Do **not** show a horizontal chip row to filter reminders by Learning project.
- Do **not** show a folder / “Link to project” control on reminder rows — Learning
  classes are not project destinations for reminders. The top filter bar must not return either.
- Do **not** show a “Linked to {{title}}” (or `todos.project_linked`) subtitle on
  reminder rows. Schedule and Learning stay separate.

## 4. No model-fallback / context-summarized chips on assistant messages
- Do **not** show `chat.model_fallback`, “switched to …”, or “N earlier messages summarized”
  chips on assistant bubbles.
- Backend may still send `fallback_used` / `context_summarized` for logging; the **mobile UI
  must not surface them**.

## 5. No empty-state body / primary CTA when a FAB already adds
- Learning and Schedule empty states: **icon + title only** (e.g. “No learning yet” / “Nothing scheduled”).
- Do **not** add body copy or an “Add …” `Button` that duplicates the bottom (+) FAB.

## 6. No image-generation confirmation sheet
- Image gen is **composer only**: user types the request and hits send; Pro generates immediately.
- Do **not** reintroduce `ImageGenPromptSheet`, attach-menu “Generate image”, or any second prompt
  modal that intercepts send. Intent detection may still call `/images/generate` — without a sheet.

## 7. No swipe-to-delete on drawer chat titles
- Do **not** wrap conversation rows in `Swipeable` / reveal a red Delete action on swipe.
- Delete stays on long-press row menu and multi-select. Schedule swipe-delete is separate.

## 8. No Lists (shopping / packing checklists)
- Do **not** add a drawer **Lists** row, list composer, `ListGroupsView`, or undated
  checklist UI. Chat must not create items without a due date.
- **Schedule** (dated reminders) stays. Learning chapter `lists` are vocab word groups,
  not this feature.

## 9. No Gmail chips or reminder bell on chat
- Do **not** show Gmail suggested-reminder chips in the composer (`SuggestedRemindersNudge`).
- Do **not** show a reminder bell on `ChatHeader`.
- Schedule keeps `SuggestedReminderRow` / From email. The drawer Schedule badge stays.

## 10. No Home dashboard chrome
- Home is **greeting + two local starters + at most one dismissible overdue row**.
- Do **not** show a Learning progress bar, due-soon stack, or “For you” personalized chips.
- Starters stay `welcomeStarters()` — ignore API `starters` / `project_highlight` on this surface.

If a plan or FEATURES item asks for these, **push back and skip** — they are explicitly rejected.
